        "---\n",
        "title: \"Fire and Smoke Lab (Alberta-first)\"\n",
        "status: \"draft\"\n",
        "id: \"labs/fire-and-smoke\"\n",
        "concepts:\n",
        "  - data-card\n",
        "  - event-windows\n",
        "  - reliability-diagram\n",
        "  - calibration\n",
        "prereq_concepts:\n",
        "  - train-test-split\n",
        "  - log-loss\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "This lab chapter turns the book’s running thread into a repeatable workflow:\n",
        "\n",
        "- find station metadata (where are the monitors?)\n",
        "- pull a long-running PM2.5 time series\n",
        "- define “smoke episodes” as event windows\n",
        "- produce a small set of visuals that you can reuse in later modelling\n",
        "\n",
        "The point is not to build the final “best” model. The point is to create a\n",
        "*disciplined dataset and evaluation story* that the mathematics in Chapters 1–8\n",
        "can attach to.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data access (OpenAQ)\n",
        "\n",
        "OpenAQ is a convenient aggregator for public air-quality monitoring data, but it\n",
        "requires a free API key. Set it as an environment variable:\n",
        "\n",
        "`OPENAQ_API_KEY=...`\n",
        "\n",
        "If the key is missing, this chapter will still render using a small synthetic\n",
        "demo dataset so the figures exist and the workflow is legible.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Station map (context first)"
      ],
      "id": "84a42a28"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| label: fig-smoke-stations\n",
        "#| fig-cap: 'A small set of PM2.5 monitoring locations pulled from OpenAQ inside the Alberta boundary (or a synthetic fallback if no API key is set). A station map is the first piece of honest context: it reveals what is measured and what is not.'\n",
        "\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import datetime as dt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib\n",
        "matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import requests\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE_URL = \"https://api.openaq.org/v3\"\n",
        "PM25_PARAMETER_ID = 2\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def _openaq_headers() -> dict:\n",
        "    api_key = os.environ.get(\"OPENAQ_API_KEY\", \"\").strip()\n",
        "    if not api_key:\n",
        "        return {}\n",
        "    return {\"X-API-Key\": api_key}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def openaq_get(path: str, params: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n",
        "    headers = _openaq_headers()\n",
        "    if not headers:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(\"Missing OPENAQ_API_KEY\")\n",
        "    url = f\"{BASE_URL}{path}\"\n",
        "    resp = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params, timeout=30)\n",
        "    resp.raise_for_status()\n",
        "    return resp.json()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def alberta_bbox() -> str:\n",
        "    # Min lon, min lat, max lon, max lat (WGS84).\n",
        "    # Broad enough to catch most Alberta monitors without being too fussy.\n",
        "    return \"-120.0,49.0,-110.0,60.0\"\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def fetch_locations_alberta(limit_per_page: int = 100, pages: int = 3) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    rows: list[dict] = []\n",
        "    for page in range(1, pages + 1):\n",
        "        payload = openaq_get(\n",
        "            \"/locations\",\n",
        "            params={\n",
        "                \"iso\": \"CA\",\n",
        "                \"bbox\": alberta_bbox(),\n",
        "                \"parameters_id\": str(PM25_PARAMETER_ID),\n",
        "                \"limit\": limit_per_page,\n",
        "                \"page\": page,\n",
        "            },\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        for loc in payload.get(\"results\", []):\n",
        "            coords = loc.get(\"coordinates\") or {}\n",
        "            rows.append(\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"location_id\": loc.get(\"id\"),\n",
        "                    \"name\": loc.get(\"name\"),\n",
        "                    \"locality\": loc.get(\"locality\"),\n",
        "                    \"provider\": (loc.get(\"provider\") or {}).get(\"name\"),\n",
        "                    \"latitude\": coords.get(\"latitude\"),\n",
        "                    \"longitude\": coords.get(\"longitude\"),\n",
        "                    \"datetime_first_local\": ((loc.get(\"datetimeFirst\") or {}).get(\"local\")),\n",
        "                    \"datetime_last_local\": ((loc.get(\"datetimeLast\") or {}).get(\"local\")),\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            )\n",
        "    df = pd.DataFrame(rows).dropna(subset=[\"latitude\", \"longitude\", \"location_id\"])\n",
        "    df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=[\"location_id\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def synthetic_locations() -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    # Fallback set: approximate coordinates for a few Alberta cities.\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "        [\n",
        "            {\"location_id\": -1, \"name\": \"Calgary (demo)\", \"locality\": \"Calgary\", \"provider\": \"demo\", \"latitude\": 51.0447, \"longitude\": -114.0719},\n",
        "            {\"location_id\": -2, \"name\": \"Edmonton (demo)\", \"locality\": \"Edmonton\", \"provider\": \"demo\", \"latitude\": 53.5461, \"longitude\": -113.4938},\n",
        "            {\"location_id\": -3, \"name\": \"Red Deer (demo)\", \"locality\": \"Red Deer\", \"provider\": \"demo\", \"latitude\": 52.2681, \"longitude\": -113.8112},\n",
        "            {\"location_id\": -4, \"name\": \"Lethbridge (demo)\", \"locality\": \"Lethbridge\", \"provider\": \"demo\", \"latitude\": 49.6935, \"longitude\": -112.8418},\n",
        "            {\"location_id\": -5, \"name\": \"Fort McMurray (demo)\", \"locality\": \"Fort McMurray\", \"provider\": \"demo\", \"latitude\": 56.7264, \"longitude\": -111.3790},\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    locations = fetch_locations_alberta()\n",
        "    source_note = \"OpenAQ\"\n",
        "except Exception:\n",
        "    locations = synthetic_locations()\n",
        "    source_note = \"synthetic fallback (set OPENAQ_API_KEY for real data)\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Pick a small set for plotting.\n",
        "locations_plot = locations.copy()\n",
        "locations_plot[\"label\"] = locations_plot[\"locality\"].fillna(locations_plot[\"name\"]).astype(str)\n",
        "locations_plot = locations_plot.sort_values([\"label\"]).head(20)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Alberta boundary (simple but geographically correct to first order: 49–60N, 110–120W).\n",
        "ab_lon = [-120.0, -110.0, -110.0, -120.0, -120.0]\n",
        "ab_lat = [49.0, 49.0, 60.0, 60.0, 49.0]\n",
        "ax.plot(ab_lon, ab_lat, color=\"#333333\", lw=1.6, label=\"Alberta boundary\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.scatter(locations_plot[\"longitude\"], locations_plot[\"latitude\"], s=28, color=\"#c44e4e\", alpha=0.85)\n",
        "for _, r in locations_plot.iterrows():\n",
        "    ax.text(r[\"longitude\"] + 0.08, r[\"latitude\"] + 0.08, str(r[\"label\"])[:18], fontsize=7, color=\"#333333\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_title(f\"Alberta-first PM2.5 stations ({source_note})\", fontsize=11)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Longitude\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Latitude\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlim(-121.5, -108.5)\n",
        "ax.set_ylim(48.0, 61.0)\n",
        "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.25)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.tight_layout()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-smoke-stations",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
