        "## Smoke-alert calibration (a decision-facing visual)\n",
        "\n",
        "A smoke alert is a *decision*, not a number. If you publish probabilities for a\n",
        "next-day smoke event, they need to be calibrated: days predicted at 30% should\n",
        "be smoke days about 30% of the time.\n",
        "\n",
        "This plot is a minimal baseline: a simple logistic model predicts next-day\n",
        "smoke-day probability from yesterday’s PM2.5 and seasonality terms. The point is\n",
        "not the model. The point is the **evaluation discipline**."
      ],
      "id": "1fd1d919"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| label: fig-smoke-calibration\n",
        "#| fig-cap: 'Reliability diagram for a baseline next-day smoke alert model. A calibrated model follows the diagonal. This is the decision-facing complement to average error: it asks whether stated probabilities match observed frequencies.'\n",
        "\n",
        "from scipy import optimize\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_next_day_dataset(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    out = df.sort_values(\"date\").copy()\n",
        "    out[\"pm25_lag1\"] = out[\"pm25\"].shift(1)\n",
        "    doy = out[\"date\"].dt.dayofyear.to_numpy()\n",
        "    out[\"sin_doy\"] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * doy / 365.25)\n",
        "    out[\"cos_doy\"] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * doy / 365.25)\n",
        "    out[\"smoke_next\"] = (out[\"pm25\"].shift(-1) >= SMOKE_THRESHOLD).astype(float)\n",
        "    out = out.dropna(subset=[\"pm25_lag1\", \"smoke_next\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def sigmoid(z: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    return 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-z))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def fit_logistic_regression(X: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    # Minimise negative log-likelihood with small L2 for numerical stability.\n",
        "    def nll(w: np.ndarray) -> float:\n",
        "        z = X @ w\n",
        "        p = sigmoid(z)\n",
        "        eps = 1e-9\n",
        "        return -np.sum(y * np.log(p + eps) + (1 - y) * np.log(1 - p + eps)) + l2 * np.sum(w * w)\n",
        "\n",
        "    w0 = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
        "    res = optimize.minimize(nll, w0, method=\"BFGS\")\n",
        "    return res.x\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "data = make_next_day_dataset(series)\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(data) < 120 or data[\"smoke_next\"].sum() < 5:\n",
        "    # Too little data to say anything honest; fall back to a synthetic reliability example.\n",
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n",
        "    p_hat = rng.uniform(0, 1, size=400)\n",
        "    y_hat = (rng.uniform(0, 1, size=400) < (0.6 * p_hat + 0.2)).astype(float)\n",
        "    title_note = \"synthetic reliability demo (insufficient real data)\"\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    # Time split: early data for training, later data for testing.\n",
        "    split = int(0.7 * len(data))\n",
        "    train = data.iloc[:split]\n",
        "    test = data.iloc[split:]\n",
        "\n",
        "    X_tr = np.column_stack(\n",
        "        [\n",
        "            np.ones(len(train)),\n",
        "            np.log1p(train[\"pm25_lag1\"].to_numpy()),\n",
        "            train[\"sin_doy\"].to_numpy(),\n",
        "            train[\"cos_doy\"].to_numpy(),\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    y_tr = train[\"smoke_next\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "\n",
